        "path": "fs/kvfs/src/node/inode.rs",
        "package": "fs/kvfs",
        "node_index": 194,
        "literal_doc_nonempty": true,
        "doc_text": " Returns the shared no-op inode operation table.\n\n The table carries no method overrides, so it inherits the trait defaults:\n DAC permission checks, the common metadata-update fallback, and rejection\n of every capability the inode does not declare. This is the counterpart of\n Linux `empty_iops`, the table `inode_init_always()` installs before a\n filesystem assigns its own.",
        "ancestor_indices": [],
        "test_path_hint": false
      },
      {
        "unit_id": "f432397c22e5fd26cdc25273f4146fe0b6e773547cdce36d797b0712508a6388",
        "path": "fs/kvfs/ut-tests/simple_file.rs",
        "package": "fs/kvfs",
        "node_index": 63,
        "literal_doc_nonempty": true,
        "doc_text": " `/proc` and `/sys` (and cgroup v2) serve their attribute files as\n `SimpleFile`s, and all three Linux file operation sets provide a poll\n operation even when the entry has no handler of its own\n (`proc_reg_file_ops`/`proc_reg_poll`, `kernfs_file_fops`/`kernfs_fop_poll`,\n both falling back to `DEFAULT_POLLMASK`). `epoll_ctl` asks only whether such\n a handler exists, so a generated file must answer yes.",
        "ancestor_indices": [],
        "test_path_hint": true
      }
    ],
